How old are you?

00:47:44.460 --> 00:47:45.340
- [Joe] 43.

00:47:45.340 --> 00:47:47.750
- So for me, you and I are part of

00:47:48.712 --> 00:47:50.650
a really interesting
generation because we're,

00:47:50.650 --> 00:47:51.563
I just turned 44.

00:47:52.970 --> 00:47:55.713
Now, I know the skinny and fats, I get it.

00:47:55.713 --> 00:47:56.717
You looked younger.

00:47:56.717 --> 00:47:57.832
You look good, bro.

00:47:57.832 --> 00:48:00.165
(laughter)

00:48:02.879 --> 00:48:04.998
One of the biggest things I'm
hoping that I can communicate

00:48:04.998 --> 00:48:07.370
to the world through
this newfound attention

00:48:08.255 --> 00:48:11.674
is our unbelievable inability

00:48:11.674 --> 00:48:14.203
to have a good relationship with time.

00:48:15.755 --> 00:48:18.090
Every 22-year-old wants
it to happen tomorrow

00:48:19.169 --> 00:48:21.914
and every 43-year-old doesn't
think that they can take

00:48:21.914 --> 00:48:24.471
a hard left and completely
start over because they don't

00:48:24.471 --> 00:48:26.013
realize they're gonna
live for another 52 years.

00:48:27.197 --> 00:48:30.890
Our complete and utter
atrocious relationship with time

00:48:30.890 --> 00:48:34.040
is leading to an enormous
amount of unhappiness

00:48:34.040 --> 00:48:37.700
and so like I see you and
even just like the energy

00:48:37.700 --> 00:48:39.150
and how you ask the question,

00:48:40.793 --> 00:48:43.132
I was compelled I'm like bro
you might just need to really

00:48:43.132 --> 00:48:44.507
look at yourself in the
mirror tonight and say,

00:48:44.507 --> 00:48:47.055
"One step backwards three steps forward."

00:48:47.055 --> 00:48:49.600
Happiness has to be the ROI you know.

00:48:49.600 --> 00:48:54.110
And I think if you could feel
in your bones another 29 years

00:48:54.110 --> 00:48:55.610
of a professional career,

00:48:55.610 --> 00:48:58.235
all of a sudden when
you look at it that way

00:48:58.235 --> 00:49:00.590
versus I'm 43 and look at all
these kids doing it at 19.

00:49:00.590 --> 00:49:04.832
If you look at it as 29 more
years before I even debate

00:49:04.832 --> 00:49:07.913
slowing down that all of
a sudden sounds practical

00:49:07.913 --> 00:49:10.800
to maybe say I don't wanna
sell widgets anymore.

00:49:10.800 --> 00:49:12.733
So that's the stuff that
goes through my mind.

00:49:13.816 --> 00:49:14.815
- [Joe] Thank you.

00:49:14.815 --> 00:49:15.648
- Yep.

00:49:18.095 --> 00:49:20.194
You can imagine you under
30 year olds in here

00:49:20.194 --> 00:49:21.140
